{"format":"hologram.registry.artifact/v1","id":"mcr.microsoft.com/microsoftgraph/powershell","fetched":"2026-09-25T12:12:15.111Z","source":{"name":"Microsoft Artifact Registry","api":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/api/v1/catalog/microsoftgraph/powershell/details?reg=mar","page":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/en-us/product/microsoftgraph/powershell/about"},"readme":"# Microsoft Graph PowerShell\n\n## About\n\nMicrosoft Graph PowerShell SDK consists of a set of commands for managing Microsoft Graph recourses directly from PowerShell.The SDK acts as an API wrapper for the Microsoft Graph APIs, exposing the entire API set for use in PowerShell. It contains a set of cmdlets that helps you manage identities at scale from automating tasks to managing users in bulk using Azure Active Directory (Azure AD). It will help administer every Azure AD feature that has an API in Microsoft Graph.\n\nMicrosoft Graph PowerShell SDK is written in .NET Standard and is supported on the supported version of PowerShell as described on the [PowerShell Support Lifecycle](https://docs.microsoft.com/powershell/scripting/powershell-support-lifecycle) page.\n\n## Featured Tags\n\n- latest `docker pull mcr.microsoft.com/microsoftgraph/powershell:latest`\n\n## Configuration\n\nPlease refer to the [getting started documentation page](https://docs.microsoft.com/powershell/microsoftgraph/get-started).\n\n## Usage\n\n`docker run -it mcr.microsoft.com/microsoftgraph/powershell:<version>`\n\nPlease refer to the [run in Docker documentation page](https://github.com/microsoftgraph/msgraph-sdk-powershell/wiki/Run-in-Docker) for more information on how to use this image.\n\n## Support\n\nIf you have any problems with or questions about this image, please contact us through a [GitHub issue](https://github.com/microsoftgraph/msgraph-sdk-powershell/issues/new).\n\n## Feedback\n\nPlease provide feedback to [Feedback](https://github.com/microsoftgraph/msgraph-sdk-powershell/issues).\n\n## License\n\n[MIT](https://github.